    "body": "Hey Daniel. 👋\r\nThank you for opening a feature request.\r\n\r\nI'm afraid such a feature would be out of scope for Starship. Instead of making such a change from within your shell's prompt, perhaps it would be best to make the per-directory change from the shell itself?\r\n\r\nI would suggest taking a look at [direnv](https://direnv.net/), which allows you to create directory-specific environment variables and executions, which lines up with what you described hooks as doing.",
